"reflection": "Waiting on the Lord is not doing nothing. It is turning toward Him again and again, the way a sail turns toward the wind. Strength comes as a gift to those who stop pretending they have their own. The desert Fathers called this watchfulness: a quiet, steady attention to God that renews us more than any rest we could plan.",
